    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A merchant republic on the lagoon, led by an elected doge and a closed hereditary nobility for about eleven centuries.</li><li>Its fleets and colonies, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>, made it the main link between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-christendom">Latin Europe</a> and the East.</li><li>Ottoman advances and new ocean routes eroded its power, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> ended the republic in 1797.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> opened the first public opera house, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teatro-san-cassiano">Teatro San Cassiano</a>, in 1637, when opera elsewhere was still largely a court entertainment.</p></aside>
    </section>

